kspalaiologos/bzip3, release 1.5.1, plus three local fixes.
Upstream: https://github.com/kspalaiologos/bzip3

libbz3.c differs from upstream 1.5.1 in three places, all inside
bz3_compress and bz3_decompress, which are the only bzip3 entry points
karyozip calls:

1. bz3_compress, block_size clamp
     ours:     if (block_size > in_size) block_size = bz3_bound(in_size);
     1.5.1:    if (block_size > in_size) block_size = in_size + 16;
   bz3_bound is the real worst case; in_size + 16 is a guess. 1.5.3 has
   adopted this one, so it is no longer a local patch against 1.5.3.

2. bz3_compress, the size of the last block
     ours:     size = (i == n_blocks - 1 ? in_size - in_offset : block_size)
     upstream: size = block_size; if (i == n_blocks - 1) size = in_size % block_size;
   The upstream form yields 0 whenever in_size is an exact multiple of
   block_size, which is every single-block call and every aligned input.
   karyozip drives bzip3 at 8 to 256 MB block sizes, so an aligned
   payload is reachable. Reproduced, lastblock_check.c: 133120 bytes at
   the 65 KiB minimum block size gives, on 1.5.3, out=1133 and 66560
   bytes back with rc=0 from both calls. Half the input, silently. Our
   copy returns all 133120 and the bytes match.

3. bz3_decompress, the per-block size check
     ours:     if (size < 0 || size > (s32)bz3_bound(block_size)) ...
     upstream: if (size < 0 || size > block_size) ...
   A block that compresses larger than its raw size is legal and fits
   bz3_bound; the upstream bound rejects it.

A fourth difference against 1.5.1, a free(compression_buf) in
bz3_decompress, upstream adopted in a later release.

DO NOT BUMP TO 1.5.3. Checked 2026-09-04: 1.5.3 still carries the
upstream form of 2 and 3, so taking it would reintroduce both. Its only
changes relative to this file are those two regressions. Re-check on the
next release with lastblock_check.c; if upstream fixes them, resync and
delete this note. Not yet reported upstream.

  gcc -O2 -DVERSION='"x"' -Ibzip3 -o lbc bzip3/lastblock_check.c \
      bzip3/libbz3.c -lpthread && ./lbc
